      ],
      "on_draft": "sticky; the PR becomes pr.merge_candidate when flipped ready"
    },
    "absorption_censoring": "p_unresolved is PRs still open at as_of; compare outcomes with p_merged_given_resolved",
    "ready_flips_note": "most draft->ready flips are scripted: see ready_flips.merged_within_60s",
    "absorption_is_chain_implied": "absorption is what the first-order chain fitted to transitions implies, not what happened: every PR in a state gets that state's average next-step mix, whatever its history. Observed outcomes differ where history matters (all 17 stuck_draft PRs later flipped ready merged, so stuck_draft merges 17/21 = 0.810 of resolved PRs against the implied 0.752). Read observed_outcomes for what happened; stuck_draft has only 21 resolved PRs, so neither figure is precise to three decimals",
    "observed_outcomes_note": "final state at as_of of the PRs whose lifecycle visits each state, same lifecycle rules and stale window; open is right-censoring. Not emitted by the ix example yet: computed from the same fixture by the independent re-implementation used to review ix#343, which reproduces every other number in this file exactly"
